invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: test/widemul-builds.sh
reason: the signer checks each candidate signature on the AVX-512 IFMA
  kernel through a declaration of its own, with no include of rsa_ifma.h.
  A wrong candidate factors n, and the kernel leaves its 512-bit
  registers in stack slots that no wipe can name, so the check must stay
  on rsa_mont64_public. The script requires that no root source but
  rsa_mont.c calls into rsa_ifma.c, whatever it includes.

--- old
    rsa_mont64_public(power, candidate, k->n_len, &mod);
--- new
    void rsa_ifma_public(uint8_t *out, const uint8_t *base, size_t len,
                         const rsa_mont64_modulus *mod, const uint64_t *digit_r2);
    rsa_ifma_public(power, candidate, k->n_len, &mod, mod.r2);
